      "date": "1907",
      "kind": "site history",
      "description": "The basement of the Robinson Apartments, at the northwest corner of Faxon and DeMontfort avenues, was used for Presbyterian services to 1906 earthquake refugees from 1907 until the first purpose-built Presbyterian church on Ocean Avenue opened in 1910 (not extant).",
